 Verify: entry_hit_tests 7/7; d2 39/39; probe 34/34; fx 20/20; phase7 68;
 phase10 61. NOT deployed.
+
+## 2026-08-10 — Restore auto signal push in the */5 scanner (F3-21, worker-only)
+
+**Bug (reviewer-verified):** Telegram auto signals stopped. The */5 scanner
+(`scheduledScan.js` scanOnePair) called `handleSignalRaw(..., { noPush: true })`
+(F3-14, added to stop scanner-push duplication while the BOT still had its own
+autoScan), and the bot v4.5.0 removed autoScan entirely (bot = thin client).
+Result: `pushSignalToSubscribers` had exactly ONE call site — manual
+`/api/signal` without `nopush` — so the scanner saved signals but never pushed
+them. Auto signals were never delivered.
+
+**Fix — Option B (simplest correct, dedup intact):** drop `noPush` at the
+scanner's call site so `handleSignalRaw -> saveAndPush` pushes. The push is
+chained behind `saveSignalToHistory`'s 30-min dedup (`{deduped}`), so a push
+fires exactly when a NEW row lands in history — no re-implemented dedup in the
+scanner. `claimPushLock` (per chat+pair+direction, 30-min TTL, same window as
+the history dedup) keeps a manual /signal call from re-pushing the same setup,
+and vice-versa. `pushLog:<signalId>` still feeds the */2 result push so only
+the subscribers who got the signal get the WIN/LOSS.
+
+Option A was rejected: its premise ("the scanner already skips duplicates via
+history dedup") does not hold — scanOnePair never sees the save result
+(`saveAndPush` runs inside `ctx.waitUntil` in handleSignalRaw), so gating on
+"new" would have required plumbing a save verdict out of the shared /api/signal
+path (bigger, riskier change) or pushing on every BUY/SELL re-poll (lock-only
+dedup). Option B reuses the existing, tested save+push chain unchanged.
+
+**Dedup verification (lock/pushLog):**
+- scanner fresh signal -> push to all matching subscribers + pushLog written;
+- re-scan of the same setup (5-min tick, inside 30-min windows) -> 0 messages
+  (history dedup) and 0 extra rows;
+- manual /signal right after a scanner push (fresh id, same pair+direction) ->
+  suppressed by claimPushLock (`skipped:'locked'`), total stays 1 message.
+
+**Files:** `src/handlers/scheduledScan.js` (call site + comments; scanOnePair
+now exported for direct testing) · `scripts/fix_tests.mjs` (T27 rewritten:
+scanner pushes fresh signal once, re-scan dedup, lock-layer re-push lockout).
+
+**Test matrix (all green):** fix_tests 277/0 (T27 +11 assertions) ·
+phase10_integration 19/19 · phase7_integration 36/36 · phase7_smoke 68/68 ·
+d2_tests 39/39 · probe_tests 34/34 · entry_hit_tests 7/7 · fx_mode_tests 20/20 ·
+r71_tests 117P/0F. E2E check through the real scheduledScan() entry point:
+first scan -> 1 Telegram message to the subscriber; second scan -> still 1;
+manual /signal -> still 1.
+
+**Bot untouched** (v4.5.0 thin client is correct). NOT deployed — manual
+worker.js rebuild + redeploy.sh required.
